<Base title="About"><div class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow on-dark">Research identity</p><h1>From laboratory science to science-of-science intelligence</h1><p>{profile.intro}</p></div></div><section class="section container"><div class="sides"><div><p class="eyebrow">Approach</p><h2>Science, data and interpretation</h2><p>I began with experimental biomedical research: culturomics, bacterial characterization and scientific writing. This domain experience provides the foundation for my work on how scientific knowledge is produced, shared, connected and translated into decisions.</p><p>My research has expanded into bibliometrics, research equity, patent landscapes, scholarly metadata engineering and applied NLP/AI. These activities connect domain science to computational approaches for making complex evidence more accessible.</p><p>The archive preserves research contributions together with software outputs, training and documentation. Not every project is finished or published; transparency about evidence and research status is part of the design.</p><h3>Opportunities & collaboration</h3><p>Interested in multidisciplinary biomedical evidence, research analytics, scientific data science, technology intelligence, or knowledge mobilization? Reach out via LinkedIn or GitHub.</p><div class="linkline"><a href={profile.linkedin}>LinkedIn ↗</a><a href={profile.github}>GitHub ↗</a><a href={profile.scholar}>Google Scholar ↗</a></div></div><aside class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Explore the archive</p><p><a href="/research/">Research domains →</a></p><p><a href="/projects/">All projects →</a></p><p><a href="/publications/">Publications →</a></p><p><a href="/credentials/">Education & certificates →</a></p><p><a href="/methods/">Methods & technical skills →</a></p><p class="source">Location: {profile.location}</p></aside></div></section></Base>
